peak-lab
========

This plugin is a Claude Code port of and derivative work from:

  leonzzz435/garmin-ai-coach
  https://github.com/leonzzz435/garmin-ai-coach
  Licensed under the MIT License.

The expert subagent system prompts in agents/metrics-expert.md,
agents/activity-expert.md, and agents/physiology-expert.md are adapted from
the corresponding metrics_expert_node.py, activity_expert_node.py, and
physiology_expert_node.py files in that project, including the
Signals / Evidence / Implications / Uncertainty framing and the two-output
contract (for_synthesis / for_weekly_planner).

The HTML dashboard layout in bin/render-analysis is inspired by the
analysis.html template from the upstream project.

At runtime, peak-lab depends on (but does not vendor) the following
third-party projects:

  cyberjunky/python-garminconnect
  https://github.com/cyberjunky/python-garminconnect
  The Python library peak-lab uses to talk to Garmin Connect directly,
  via the bundled CLIs `bin/fetch-garmin` (bulk pulls) and
  `bin/garmin-call` (single-method read-only drill-downs). Resolved at
  runtime through uv's PEP 723 inline script dependencies; not bundled
  with this plugin.

Name disambiguation
-------------------

"peak-lab" is an independent third-party plugin and is **not** affiliated with,
endorsed by, or connected to Garmin Ltd. or its "Garmin Coach" adaptive
training plan feature. The plugin analyzes data exported from Garmin Connect
but is not a Garmin product.
